 Only the Lead can create teammates or interrupt them.
 
+Programmatic `spawnTeammate` calls may pass `agentOptions` for the child LLM provider, model, and reasoning effort. The request's `provider` still identifies the continuation transport (`spawn` or `fork`). The existing subagent descriptor records the effective child route and restores it when a stored teammate receives another message; changing the Lead's route does not reroute an existing member. Model-facing selection policy and live route validation belong to the Team tool package, before provisioning reserves a name.
+
 ### Messages between teammates
 
 Any member can send to another member or the Lead. Each attempt either returns the target inbox `MessageId` or throws. Team does not retain unaccepted send intent, retry new messages after restart, or deduplicate explicit resends.
