+### Task-aware model selection
+
+Enable `modelSelectionSettings: true` alongside the Host's `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent/model-selection-settings`, with that Host setting's `enabled: true` and exact `allowedModels`. New Sessions capture their authority durably; existing Sessions without captured authority remain disabled. Changing Host settings does not expand existing Session authority.
+
+The Lead selects `specialist` from the task: `designer`, `researcher`, `engineer`, `architect`, or `verifier`. The optional `models` map contains configurable preferences, not measured model rankings:
+
+```yaml
+config:
+  freshProvider: spawn
+  forkProvider: fork
+  modelSelectionSettings: true
+  models:
+    engineer:
+      provider: your-llm-provider
+      model: your-model-id
+      reasoningEffort: high
+```
+
+An explicit `provider` and `model` pair on `spawn_teammate`, plus optional `reasoning_effort`, overrides the preference. Changing the explicit route without an effort uses the selected model's default effort. A missing preference inherits compatible parent values. `freshProvider` and `forkProvider` select subagent transport; `models.*.provider` selects the LLM provider.
+
+Both preferences and explicit selection must pass the Session allowlist and live adapter preflight. Unknown providers, invalid models, disallowed routes, and unsupported efforts fail before creating a roster member or reserving its name; no fallback model is substituted. Enabled Lead scopes register `list_subagent_models` once for route and effort discovery. The child descriptor retains its selected route and effort for cold restoration.
+
+### Local same-release builds
+
+For a desktop running this exact package release, [build-specialist-team-local.ts](../../../scripts/build-specialist-team-local.ts) accepts `--runtime <installed-dsh-root>` and `--out <local-plugin-directory>`. It checks the installed Team version and emits the Team service, Team tools, and ordinary subagent tools with shared model-selection helpers; other peers resolve through the installed runtime. Override the existing profile entry names with these local modules and retain their full configuration. Restart DSH and use a new Session to activate model selection; existing Session authority is preserved. This is a release-specific backport, not a replacement for a full desktop upgrade.
+
